From 0ae229feabe9dcf526312e9b97cec1b0110fd093 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:21:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): placement config falls back to the board home's
 block [daveey]

kanban_placement.config() read kanban.placement only from the active
profile's config.yaml. The managed worker profiles (bb-tuner, coach,
alpha-follow) carry a kanban: section with no placement block, so under
them config() was {}: a portable card they created on a pool worker never
got runs_on [pool:worker], extra_home_markers / hub_read_roots were not
applied, and destinations({}) was empty (t_01a1d8146b9ef790 kept local
with 'needs worker coordination capability').

The board is shared by every profile on the host (kanban_db.kanban_home()),
so its placement policy is a machine fact carried by the board home's
config.yaml, the same place kanban_capabilities, kanban_db_sync and
kanban_gate_only already read board-wide policy from. config() now uses
the active profile's non-empty block when there is one (it wins whole, no
per-key merge) and otherwise the board home's. A config_snapshot pins the
fallback block like any other.

Chosen over provisioning a placement copy into each managed profile from
hermes-state: a copy goes stale whenever the root block changes, and it
would cover only install-profiles.py's three worker profiles, not hub or
Mac profiles that create cards on the same board.

Proof (worker-7, HERMES_HOME=~/.hermes/profiles/bb-tuner, read-only
kp.decide + _local_placement for a host-neutral portable bb-tuner card):
  live core:  placement keys [], queue_label None,
              local 'assignee not allowlisted', no runs_on
  this patch: queue_label pool:worker, runs_on ['pool:worker'],
              'portable: queued for any machine labelled pool:worker'

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_placement_board_home.py (3 of 5 RED
on main, 5/5 GREEN here).

Refs t_01a1db0fb5d6a9cc
